1
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:35,000
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,740
[Episode 33]

3
00:01:38,590 --> 00:01:40,000
Your collegial panel's decision
to impose a suspended death sentence

4
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,710
is internally contradictory.

5
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:43,920
The defendant recanted
his earlier confession in court,

6
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:44,770
showed a hostile attitude,

7
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:46,450
and refused to pay compensation.

8
00:01:46,450 --> 00:01:47,479
There isn't

9
00:01:47,509 --> 00:01:49,310
a single mitigating factor here,

10
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:50,680
yet you still gave him
a suspended death sentence?

11
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,350
Isn't this basically admitting

12
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:54,479
we lack confidence in our own verdict?

13
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,890
In the old days,

14
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,590
this would unquestionably
have been a death sentence.

15
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:00,090
Of course, there are flaws.

16
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:00,530
But

17
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,680
not every case has

18
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:02,760
perfect evidence.

19
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,760
If we give him a suspended death sentence,

20
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,720
the victim's family

21
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:05,720
will be up in arms.

22
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,350
Then sentence him to death.

23
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:07,480
I have no objection.

24
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,100
Deputy Court Pres. Yu.

25
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,780
Why do I get the feeling that you're

26
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:24,750
being a little negative?

27
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:26,079
I'm not being negative.

28
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:28,430
Giving him a suspended death sentence
isn't about lacking confidence.

29
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:29,560
It's out of caution.

30
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:31,710
It leaves some leeway for our court.

31
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,520
Qian Xingliang's case

32
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,720
wasn't that long ago.

33
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,980
It's still fresh
in our memories, comrades.

34
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,100
I reserve my position.

35
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,870
I don't think there's much of a problem
with this case.

36
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:49,630
Let's vote.

37
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:53,490
Jia Peng.

38
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,570
Who exactly did you hear

39
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:00,610
about Lin Yan's case from?

40
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:03,190
From whom?

41
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:05,680
From myself.

42
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,240
You don't seriously think

43
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,170
all these antics

44
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,330
are going to save your life, do you?

45
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:16,030
No.

46
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,030
Jia Peng,

47
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:20,030
your death sentence has been

48
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,160
approved on review.

49
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,310
It'll be carried out in a few days.

50
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:25,280
Don't you want to

51
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,760
earn yourself some good karma...

52
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,430
and leave a tiny bit

53
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:33,560
of goodness in your life?

54
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:40,030
No.

55
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:46,680
Never even crossed my mind.

56
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:51,079
Do you know...

57
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,310
what my biggest regret in life

58
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,030
is?

59
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,480
That I never killed my dad
with my own hands—

60
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,820
which let him go on ruining my mom's life.

61
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,540
How about this?

62
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,920
You bring him here,

63
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,820
and let me kill him myself.

64
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,310
Then I'll tell you

65
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:22,480
exactly what happened to Lin Yan,

66
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:22,830
okay?

67
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:25,360
So someone did

68
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,480
tell you the details of the crime scene,

69
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,210
didn't they?

70
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,440
Right.

71
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:33,310
Who?

72
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,430
Guess.

73
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:45,159
Getting angry, are you?

74
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,240
She's angry.

75
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:52,540
You know what?

76
00:04:52,650 --> 00:04:53,800
Seeing you people get angry

77
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,840
makes me especially happy.

78
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:55,340
Really.

79
00:05:08,330 --> 00:05:11,570
[Anti-Corruption and Bribery Bureau]
[Nanlu Municipal People's Procuratorate]

80
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,680
Chief Prosecutor,

81
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,920
can we discuss it again

82
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,510
with them

83
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,130
and postpone the execution for a few days?

84
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:17,740
Lihui.

85
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:21,920
You're a prosecutor yourself.

86
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,600
Do you really not understand?

87
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,560
Because of this case,

88
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,360
Jia Peng's execution
has already been postponed.

89
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:29,270
So many people are already
on the hook for that.

90
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:31,240
What if, while waiting for execution,

91
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:31,800
Jia Peng

92
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,870
commits suicide

93
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:33,930
or dies of illness,

94
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,950
or what if something else

95
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:35,950
g-goes wrong?

96
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:38,680
Who will take responsibility?

97
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:40,810
Chief Prosecutor,

98
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,630
let's just discuss it with them again

99
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:45,040
and ask them to postpone it
for a few more days.

100
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,100
Chief Prosecutor.

101
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:48,720
Lihui.

102
00:05:50,070 --> 00:05:50,950
Even now,

103
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:52,280
you still won't give up?

104
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:53,520
Do you know

105
00:05:53,630 --> 00:05:55,550
how many people finally felt a huge weight

106
00:05:55,550 --> 00:05:56,430
lifted from their shoulders

107
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:58,430
when the DNA test results came back?

108
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,190
After deliberation
by this court's Judicial Committee,

109
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:03,680
the following judgment is hereby rendered:

110
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,160
First,

111
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,480
the defendant, Hu Xudong,

112
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,180
is guilty of intentional homicide

113
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,640
and is sentenced to death,

114
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,700
with deprivation of
political rights for life.

115
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:14,110
Second...

116
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:14,800
I didn't kill him.

117
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,620
The defendant, Hu Xudong,

118
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:17,070
shall compensate the plaintiff
in the incidental civil action...

119
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:17,870
It wasn't me!

120
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,460
I didn't kill him!

121
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:21,090
How can you rule like this?

122
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,610
Court is adjourned.

123
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:24,950
I didn't do it!

124
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:27,030
How can you sentence me like this?

125
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:27,720
Dad! Dad!

126
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,120
Dad, Dad, are you alright?

127
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,950
How can you sentence me like this?

128
00:06:30,950 --> 00:06:32,070
Are you alright, Dad? Dad!

129
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,070
Is it your heart, Dad?

130
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:33,630
Dad!

131
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:34,870
Dad, it's okay!

132
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,070
Dad! Dad!

133
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,000
Hu Xujie,

134
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:37,870
tell Dad

135
00:06:38,159 --> 00:06:39,159
we won't pay a single cent.

136
00:06:39,159 --> 00:06:39,960
Do you hear me?

137
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,090
Not a single cent!

138
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,120
Xudong, don't worry!

139
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,050
I want to appeal!

140
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,650
I want to appeal.

141
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,730
I want to appeal!

142
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:46,950
I want to appeal!

143
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:48,800
I want to appeal!

144
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:50,430
Mr. Chen,

145
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,170
as a member of the victim's family,

146
00:06:53,310 --> 00:06:54,120
I despise you.

147
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:55,880
But as a journalist,

148
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:57,190
I admire you.

149
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,310
Mr. Chen.

150
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:06,930
Is your dad okay?

151
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:08,310
My dad is fine.

152
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:17,470
My dad asked me to tell you

153
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:18,680
that we'll still be hiring you

154
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:20,680
as our lawyers for the second trial.

155
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:21,720
Thank you.

156
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,130
Thank you, Mr. Chen.

157
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:28,030
Thank you.

158
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,240
Dad.

159
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:32,820
Are you alright, Dad?

160
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,870
What's wrong with me drinking?

161
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:48,480
I'll drink if I want!

162
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,630
I've had enough of you
nagging me all day, every day!

163
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:51,720
How dare you tell me what to do!

164
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,870
How dare you tell me what to do!

165
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:54,000
I'll drink if I want!

166
00:07:54,310 --> 00:07:55,600
You just won't let me

167
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:56,800
live in peace!

168
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,200
I'll drink if I want!

169
00:07:58,630 --> 00:07:59,159
Who is it?

170
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,330
We're from the procuratorate.

171
00:08:05,510 --> 00:08:05,950
Hello.

172
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,390
Who are you looking for?

173
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:10,120
We're looking for Jia Peng's mother.

174
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:10,780
She's dead.

175
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:12,800
Dead?

176
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,750
Then you should report that to the police.

177
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:15,870
Who killed her? You?

178
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:16,530
Who are you?

179
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,200
Stop talking nonsense here.

180
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,620
I'm Jia Peng's father!

181
00:08:24,610 --> 00:08:26,010
Xi Fenglan, are you home?

182
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:26,830
Your son, Jia Peng,

183
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:28,160
asked us to come see you!

184
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:29,970
Xi Fenglan!

185
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:30,830
What are you doing?

186
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:31,870
Xi Fenglan, are you home?

187
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,000
What are you doing?

188
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:33,780
Stay still.

189
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,030
You might hurt yourself!

190
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:36,240
They're attacking me!

191
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,390
They're attacking me!

192
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,440
Let go. Let go of him.

193
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:38,970
Jianmin!

194
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:40,340
You can't reason with people like him.

195
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:41,390
I'm Xi Fenglan.

196
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,790
Has my son Jia Peng...

197
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,870
not been executed yet?

198
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:55,210
W-Wait a moment!

199
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,240
Don't hang up yet!

200
00:09:00,150 --> 00:09:01,240
Wait a moment! Wait!

201
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,680
Um... Mr. Chen is here too.

202
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:03,840
Tell both of us at the same time.

203
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:04,670
Alright, go ahead!

204
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:05,470
Speak louder!

205
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:08,310
In Hu Xudong's case,

206
00:09:08,310 --> 00:09:09,760
a new witness has come forward.

207
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,240
The Provincial High Court will very likely

208
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:13,020
send the case back for a retrial.

209
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:13,720
You should be receiving

210
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,320
official notice very soon as well.

211
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,150
That's all. I won't say more.

212
00:09:17,170 --> 00:09:17,700
Goodbye.

213
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,840
Okay, okay, okay!

214
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,260
Who was that? What's going on?

215
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,370
Yizhong,

216
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,390
do you think the Qian Xingliang incident

217
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:27,550
will repeat itself?

218
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,130
What do you mean, "repeat"?

219
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:32,270
This time,

220
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,120
Yu Gaoyuan is

221
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,270
really going to have a rough time of it.

222
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:36,130
Let's go have a drink tonight too.

223
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:38,790
Why did you wait until now

224
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:39,650
to report this?

225
00:09:40,030 --> 00:09:41,480
When he was still alive,

226
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,720
I was scared

227
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,160
and didn't dare to say anything.

228
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,910
Later, he got into a fight

229
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,690
and was beaten to death.

230
00:09:49,870 --> 00:09:51,910
He was released from prison 3 years ago.

231
00:09:51,910 --> 00:09:53,170
He couldn't find a job,

232
00:09:53,630 --> 00:09:55,720
so he started doing odd jobs for people
—running errands,

233
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:59,250
intimidating others, settling disputes,
or things like that.

234
00:09:59,790 --> 00:10:00,960
Come on, drink!

235
00:10:06,870 --> 00:10:07,320
Boss!

236
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:08,240
Boss!

237
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,380
What's going on, Boss?

238
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:21,270
I thought he was already dead,

239
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:23,550
so what was the point of me
saying anything?

240
00:10:23,550 --> 00:10:25,440
It wasn't until a couple of days ago,
when I saw the news,

241
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,720
that I learned someone
had been sentenced to death.

242
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,050
Then it suddenly hit me—

243
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,450
could it be

244
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,340
the crime he'd committed before?

245
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:35,440
Wouldn't that mean an innocent person
had been wrongly convicted?

246
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,480
At first, I didn't want to
bring trouble upon myself.

247
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,210
But everyone has a conscience.

248
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,840
I really couldn't sleep.

249
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:44,650
Besides, that man is already dead.

250
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:46,240
He got what he deserved.

251
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:48,100
So why let someone else

252
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,440
die in his place?

253
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:51,040
Just isn't worth it.

254
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,180
Just based on this?

255
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:56,790
This woman is Li Fengqin.

256
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,500
The real culprit, she claimed,

257
00:10:58,500 --> 00:10:59,430
was Du Changjun,

258
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,020
her ex-boyfriend.

259
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:04,240
Du Changjun, Yin Ping,

260
00:11:04,270 --> 00:11:05,030
and Hu Xudong

261
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:05,840
were all

262
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,030
from the same village.

263
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:08,490
They all knew one another.

264
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:09,720
But Du Changjun

265
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:10,910
didn't actually live in the village.

266
00:11:10,910 --> 00:11:12,730
He'd been hanging around town for years.

267
00:11:12,730 --> 00:11:13,550
On October 17th,

268
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:14,840
at 11:40 PM,

269
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:16,780
Du Changjun killed Yin Ping

270
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:17,840
by the irrigation canal.

271
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,850
He was covered in blood

272
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:19,910
and fled that very night

273
00:11:19,910 --> 00:11:21,510
to Li Fengqin's home in town.

274
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,330
What about the bloody clothes?

275
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,260
The murder weapon?

276
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:28,030
The bloody clothes
were burned that same night.

277
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:29,030
As for the weapon, it was supposedly

278
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:30,640
discarded somewhere near the crime scene—

279
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:31,760
a modified

280
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:32,600
Type 56 military bayonet.

281
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,790
But there's no way to find it now.

282
00:11:33,790 --> 00:11:34,910
That canal has been filled in

283
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:36,030
and turned into a road.

284
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,760
Why did he want to kill Yin Ping?

285
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:46,130
The man at the fertilizer depot named...

286
00:11:47,630 --> 00:11:48,360
named Liu.

287
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,040
They got into a fight over money.

288
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:52,720
Liu reported him,

289
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,330
so he was detained for 15 days.

290
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,440
He held a grudge

291
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:59,110
and wanted to get back at Liu,

292
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:02,100
so he hid by the canal
waiting for him to get off work.

293
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,920
Then why did he kill Yin Ping?

294
00:12:04,910 --> 00:12:06,440
He killed the wrong person.

295
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:07,800
He told me

296
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:09,150
that he saw someone coming

297
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:10,410
and assumed it was Liu.

298
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:12,840
His first stab struck him
in the lower back.

299
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:19,200
Move!

300
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:30,680
Changjun...

301
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,260
We specifically
had the police check again.

302
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:03,980
Du Changjun was left-handed.

303
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:06,000
Yu,

304
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:07,950
you really called it.

305
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,240
Another Qian Xingliang.

306
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:12,080
Fortunately, she came forward

307
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,010
while the case was still on appeal.

308
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:13,910
A couple more months

309
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:14,390
and we'd

310
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:15,670
have been in real trouble.

311
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:16,600
Thank goodness.

312
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:18,790
That still doesn't prove

313
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:20,050
Hu Xudong is innocent.

314
00:13:20,810 --> 00:13:21,960
Everything Li Fengqin said

315
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,420
lines up with the details.

316
00:13:26,030 --> 00:13:27,290
Where's the evidence?

317
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:37,510
Yu,

318
00:13:38,550 --> 00:13:40,200
I really can't figure you out.

319
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,930
What exactly are you thinking?

320
00:13:45,630 --> 00:13:46,560
Court Pres. Qiu,

321
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:48,750
now we're trying to

322
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:50,360
correct a wrongful conviction.

323
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,440
Above all else,

324
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,380
the case must be decided on the evidence.

325
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,880
When all is said and done,

326
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:58,010
evidence is what matters.

327
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:06,550
With a bowl of wine from Mom
before I leave,

328
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:09,630
I'm filled with courage...

329
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:24,720
Mom?

330
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,000
Son...

331
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:36,510
Mom.

332
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:37,910
Mom.

333
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:44,630
-My son!
-Mom! Mom!

334
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:45,150
Mom...

335
00:14:48,270 --> 00:14:50,600
-Mom.
-It's all my fault!

336
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:52,790
I'm sorry, my son!

337
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:53,260
Mom!

338
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,150
My son.

339
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:57,510
I thought you didn't want me anymore.

340
00:15:01,550 --> 00:15:04,200
I'll never abandon you, son.

341
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:05,120
Mom.

342
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,450
I'll never abandon you.

343
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,270
Did that bastard

344
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:10,200
hit you again?

345
00:15:12,630 --> 00:15:13,230
It's fine.

346
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:14,120
I'm fine.

347
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,390
I'm fine.

348
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:16,750
My son...

349
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:25,960
Mom.

350
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:27,040
My son...

351
00:15:30,390 --> 00:15:30,870
Mom.

352
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:35,750
Now that you're here,

353
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:37,960
I can leave in peace.

354
00:15:38,530 --> 00:15:39,570
Don't go...

355
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:48,550
Son...

356
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,580
Mom wants to ask you for one thing.

357
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:58,870
That video alone is

358
00:15:58,870 --> 00:16:01,240
more than enough to show
what really happened.

359
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,150
Do you still believe

360
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:03,750
Hu Xudong is the real killer?

361
00:16:04,390 --> 00:16:05,850
I understand how you feel.

362
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,840
But as a legal professional,

363
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,320
everything must follow
proper procedure and be based on evidence.

364
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,320
Presiding Judge,

365
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,030
the only evidence in this case
worth considering

366
00:16:14,030 --> 00:16:15,150
is that bloody shirt.

367
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:16,480
I've said it many times—

368
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:20,080
blood types can only rule someone out;
they can't confirm identity.

369
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,360
Even if the blood type matches,

370
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,390
you still can't prove

371
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:23,990
that it was Yin Ping's blood.

372
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,660
I agree.

373
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:26,650
You agree?

374
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:34,750
You can apply for
a new forensic examination

375
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:35,810
to compare the DNA.

376
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:41,920
The application for re-examination.

377
00:16:47,790 --> 00:16:49,650
Yin Ping has already been buried.

378
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,240
The existing samples

379
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,300
aren't sufficient for a new DNA test.

380
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,140
If you want a re-examination,

381
00:16:55,270 --> 00:16:56,720
the police will have to

382
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,280
supervise the exhumation.

383
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:02,330
You know Yin Ping's uncle
isn't someone easy to deal with.

384
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:04,240
We'll coordinate with
the police department;

385
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:07,099
mediating between the two parties
will be your job.

386
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:25,720
Fifty thousand yuan?

387
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,460
For exhuming the body for an autopsy?

388
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,480
Our Xudong

389
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,470
never killed anyone in that family.

390
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:34,070
Why should we pay this money?

391
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:36,770
Wouldn't that basically
be admitting guilt?

392
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:39,280
If Yin Ping's uncle doesn't agree,

393
00:17:40,510 --> 00:17:42,240
there's nothing anyone can do.

394
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:42,830
After all,

395
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:44,360
it's part of our tradition:

396
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,720
the dead must be treated
with the utmost respect.

397
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,380
Isn't everything we're doing

398
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,750
meant to prove

399
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:51,210
Hu Xudong didn't kill him?

400
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:53,720
You know
what his family's situation is like.

401
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,550
This is already
a huge gesture of sincerity.

402
00:17:55,550 --> 00:17:56,510
If you agree,

403
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,720
just sign here.

404
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,740
What kind of person do you take me for?

405
00:18:04,030 --> 00:18:05,160
Do you really not care

406
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,250
who the real killer is?

407
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:07,790
Do you truly believe Hu Xudong

408
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:08,790
is not the killer?

409
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,090
I absolutely do.

410
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:14,750
I heard you once advised him
to plead guilty.

411
00:18:15,110 --> 00:18:16,230
Wouldn't that contradict

412
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:18,790
the so-called inner conviction
you legal professionals talk about?

413
00:18:18,790 --> 00:18:20,000
I'm a lawyer.

414
00:18:20,490 --> 00:18:22,240
My professional ethics require me

415
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,510
to do everything I can

416
00:18:23,530 --> 00:18:25,160
to protect my client's interests.

417
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,240
To keep him alive,

418
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,810
I had to compromise.

419
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:30,110
And I had to persuade him
to compromise too.

420
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:31,160
There's no contradiction in that.

421
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:31,920
So,

422
00:18:32,030 --> 00:18:32,830
the truth

423
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,510
isn't

424
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,830
the most important thing to you?

425
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:38,000
Precisely because

426
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,750
I believe in the truth,

427
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:42,750
I can compromise

428
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:44,430
with a clear conscience.

429
00:18:45,030 --> 00:18:45,890
What about you?

430
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,960
Are you willing to give the truth

431
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:49,020
a chance?

432
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,510
Did Yu Gaoyuan approve the application
for the exhumation?

433
00:18:53,510 --> 00:18:54,000
Yes.

434
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,750
Yin Ping's uncle

435
00:18:55,750 --> 00:18:57,080
also signed and agreed.

436
00:18:57,150 --> 00:18:58,350
What happens after the exhumation?

437
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:00,200
I've contacted
Peking Union Medical College Hospital.

438
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:00,960
They're qualified

439
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:01,920
for DNA testing.

440
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:04,270
It's just that the cost is extremely high.

441
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:05,130
Too expensive,

442
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,200
and it takes too long, doesn't it?

443
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:06,600
Right.

444
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:08,000
And Hu Xudong's family

445
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,590
can't come up with the money either.

446
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:11,320
In the end, Lu and I discussed it

447
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,290
and decided we'd pay for it ourselves.

448
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:16,550
You two have money to burn or something?

449
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:17,880
If everyone handled cases like you,

450
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,140
all of us legal workers

451
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,500
would starve to death.

452
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,570
It's not like we do this every time.

453
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:26,700
What's this?

454
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,770
[Forensic Examination Authorization]

455
00:19:27,530 --> 00:19:29,480
Dongjiang Provincial People's Procuratorate.

456
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,650
The Ministry of Public Security's
Physical Evidence Identification Center...

457
00:19:31,650 --> 00:19:32,790
This is a special appraisal fund

458
00:19:32,790 --> 00:19:33,880
for major cases.

459
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,590
Twenty-eight thousand yuan.

460
00:19:35,590 --> 00:19:36,310
The provincial procuratorate

461
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,400
has already transferred it.

462
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,550
After the exhumation,

463
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:39,110
the samples

464
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:42,770
will be frozen and transported directly
to Beijing under escort.

465
00:19:43,110 --> 00:19:44,040
For the witness line,

466
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:44,790
sign your name here.

467
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:45,640
Just write

468
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,570
"defense technical consultant."

469
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:48,030
Okay.

470
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:50,160
The provincial procuratorate

471
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:50,720
has already spoken

472
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:51,750
with the Ministry of Public Security.

473
00:19:51,750 --> 00:19:52,720
They'll bump it up the queue,

474
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,650
so it probably won't take too long.

475
00:19:59,480 --> 00:19:59,940
Mentor,

476
00:20:01,110 --> 00:20:02,000
aren't you afraid this money

477
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,220
will be wasted in the end?

478
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:03,880
I want to confirm his guilt

479
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,140
more than anyone else.

480
00:20:05,510 --> 00:20:06,550
But if it means

481
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,090
upholding a death sentence

482
00:20:08,090 --> 00:20:09,240
based on flawed evidence,

483
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,100
I won't be able to retire in peace.

484
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:12,720
If this money

485
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:14,640
can really buy us conclusive evidence,

486
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:16,700
then it will be money very well spent.

487
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:20,750
Hu.

488
00:20:21,590 --> 00:20:22,250
Let's do it.

489
00:20:24,270 --> 00:20:25,130
Start digging!

490
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:25,880
Be careful!

491
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:28,690
Yin Ping,

492
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,480
we've come to seek justice for you!

493
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:30,940
Come on!

494
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:53,140
Please eat.

495
00:20:53,950 --> 00:20:54,830
This chicken is pretty good.

496
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:55,640
No need.

497
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:57,870
I'll eat with my husband

498
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:58,750
later.

499
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:01,440
Okay.

500
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,510
On the day of the execution,

501
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:06,350
did you go?

502
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,070
I did.

503
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,280
I brought him

504
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:14,920
his favorite hard candy—

505
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,470
the peanut-flavored kind.

506
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:19,550
But they wouldn't let him eat it.

507
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,330
They just took him away.

508
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:35,110
My Peng really had

509
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:37,960
such a miserable life.

510
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:40,160
Since he was little,

511
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,140
he'd been beaten by his dad...

512
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,350
and by his classmates.

513
00:21:54,590 --> 00:21:55,920
Please don't be too sad.

514
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:00,600
Then...

515
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:04,140
did you ask him
what we wanted you to find out?

516
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,120
In the next few days, we...

517
00:22:26,050 --> 00:22:26,720
I'm sorry.

518
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,400
Chief Prosecutor...

519
00:22:29,870 --> 00:22:31,070
Let's leave it here for today.

520
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:32,590
I need to talk to Lihui about something.

521
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:32,920
Okay.

522
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:37,400
Lihui,

523
00:22:37,750 --> 00:22:38,510
come on, sit.

524
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,000
That case of yours is

525
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,070
on hold for now.

526
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:43,900
Just focus on your work...

527
00:22:44,270 --> 00:22:45,070
Wei Heshui.

528
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:48,820
That man's name is Wei Heshui.

529
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:50,930
What Wei Heshui?

530
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Before Jia Peng was executed,

531
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
he told his mother

532
00:22:54,530 --> 00:22:55,480
that the person who had told him

533
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,270
the details of Lin Yan's case

534
00:22:56,270 --> 00:22:58,160
was a fellow inmate named Wei Heshui.

535
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,160
But Wei Heshui only told him the details,

536
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,420
not the whole process.

537
00:23:00,550 --> 00:23:02,070
That would completely explain

538
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:02,900
why Jia Peng's account

539
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,050
of the whole process

540
00:23:04,110 --> 00:23:04,880
didn't add up,

541
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,000
yet when it came to the details,

542
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,730
he was surprisingly accurate.

543
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:09,960
Lihui.

544
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:12,590
I really think you've become

545
00:23:12,590 --> 00:23:13,720
obsessed with this.

546
00:23:14,350 --> 00:23:15,610
You're taking the word

547
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,410
of a death-row inmate seriously?

548
00:23:17,410 --> 00:23:18,440
Maybe I really have

549
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,440
become obsessed.

550
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,440
But perhaps Wei Heshui

551
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,310
is actually the real killer of Lin Yan.

552
00:23:22,310 --> 00:23:23,960
Can we take this seriously

553
00:23:24,270 --> 00:23:25,400
and investigate it?

554
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,540
Chief Prosecutor.

555
00:23:30,110 --> 00:23:30,510
Sit.

556
00:23:36,110 --> 00:23:38,000
Please investigate it a little further,

557
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:38,480
okay?

558
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:54,080
Hello.

559
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:55,700
Check immediately

560
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:56,980
whether any inmate

561
00:23:57,170 --> 00:23:58,440
held at the detention center

562
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:59,550
at the same time as Jia Peng

563
00:23:59,550 --> 00:24:00,790
was named...

564
00:24:00,830 --> 00:24:01,490
Wei Heshui.

565
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,680
Wei Heshui.

566
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:03,830
Yes.

567
00:24:04,550 --> 00:24:05,680
If he's still in custody,

568
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:07,170
find out which prison he's in.

569
00:24:07,170 --> 00:24:08,500
Compile all his records

570
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:09,850
and bring them to me.

571
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:10,720
Yes,

572
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:11,760
immediately.

573
00:24:14,510 --> 00:24:16,170
Thank you, Chief Prosecutor.

574
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,110
I really don't know what to say.

575
00:24:21,110 --> 00:24:21,720
I just...

576
00:24:23,290 --> 00:24:23,880
Lihui,

577
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,570
there's one more thing.

578
00:24:27,690 --> 00:24:28,800
After I tell you,

579
00:24:28,830 --> 00:24:30,560
you'll need to brace yourself.

580
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:32,150
You may already be

581
00:24:32,150 --> 00:24:33,750
mentally prepared for this.

582
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:35,830
This morning,

583
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,440
Prosecutor You called me.

584
00:24:42,310 --> 00:24:43,410
This morning,

585
00:24:44,310 --> 00:24:45,510
Comrade Guo Dajie...

586
00:24:46,590 --> 00:24:47,320
passed away.

587
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:52,070
Lihui,

588
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,860
I hope you find the strength
to get through this.

589
00:24:59,310 --> 00:24:59,790
Lihui.

590
00:25:01,790 --> 00:25:02,320
Lihui...

591
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:06,360
Hello?

592
00:25:09,110 --> 00:25:10,710
Bring the records over regardless.

593
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:11,160
Yes.

594
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:22,550
Lihui.

595
00:25:25,590 --> 00:25:26,960
It's just been confirmed

596
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:27,960
that Wei Heshui

597
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:29,660
was indeed detained

598
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:31,000
in the same detention center

599
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,730
as Jia Peng for a period of time.

600
00:25:32,790 --> 00:25:33,880
But he was

601
00:25:34,590 --> 00:25:35,990
released half a year ago.

602
00:25:36,410 --> 00:25:38,070
The procuratorate will request
the public security department

603
00:25:38,070 --> 00:25:40,070
to investigate as soon as possible.

604
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:37,680
Mr. Yuan,

605
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:40,220
the...

606
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:42,440
the fact that you're willing to

607
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,170
come see me and defend me...

608
00:26:46,830 --> 00:26:48,110
I'm really happy.

609
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:51,480
I really am.

610
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:53,310
Qin.

611
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:57,240
I agreed to represent you

612
00:26:58,350 --> 00:27:00,480
because I wanted to hear

613
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:02,960
your account of

614
00:27:03,270 --> 00:27:04,130
what happened.

615
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,270
I did it deliberately.

616
00:27:12,890 --> 00:27:15,440
Although I regretted it afterward,

617
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:18,920
I really did intend to

618
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:20,920
commit the crime.

619
00:27:23,590 --> 00:27:24,480
I'd looked into

620
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:26,000
that pesticide's

621
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:28,510
properties beforehand.

622
00:27:29,510 --> 00:27:31,350
I bought it to drink myself,

623
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:34,060
but she snatched it away and drank it.

624
00:27:35,350 --> 00:27:37,880
I watched my wife slowly die

625
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,880
from the pesticide with my own eyes.

626
00:27:45,350 --> 00:27:46,410
And I deliberately

627
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,850
delayed getting her medical help.

628
00:28:00,240 --> 00:28:01,550
She ruined my life,

629
00:28:03,790 --> 00:28:05,680
ruined the last bit of hope I had.

630
00:28:06,830 --> 00:28:07,510
In the end,

631
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:10,030
the two of us...

632
00:28:12,030 --> 00:28:13,160
went down together.

633
00:28:16,690 --> 00:28:18,490
This is karmic retribution.

634
00:28:21,790 --> 00:28:24,240
I only wish
my daughter hadn't had to suffer.

635
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:25,070
Xiaowen...

636
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,530
It's your daughter Xiaowen

637
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,380
who has asked me to defend you.

638
00:28:39,830 --> 00:28:41,640
My daughter has forgiven me?

639
00:28:48,720 --> 00:28:49,880
I'm guilty.

640
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,900
Mr. Yuan, I deserve to die.

641
00:28:55,350 --> 00:28:56,280
I deserve to die.

642
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,000
I haven't even represented you

643
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,750
in court yet.

644
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:01,350
Qin,

645
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:04,440
I've seen what your life with your wife

646
00:29:04,590 --> 00:29:05,400
was like.

647
00:29:06,750 --> 00:29:07,480
And I know...

648
00:29:09,510 --> 00:29:10,710
as a lawyer yourself,

649
00:29:11,790 --> 00:29:12,990
you know the law well.

650
00:29:13,590 --> 00:29:14,750
So why did you do it?

651
00:29:18,830 --> 00:29:20,230
I turned myself in twice.

652
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:22,570
It's all written clearly in the case file.

653
00:29:23,030 --> 00:29:24,440
There's no need

654
00:29:25,550 --> 00:29:28,210
for a great lawyer like you
to defend me anymore.

655
00:29:36,030 --> 00:29:37,210
The highlight

656
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,680
of my entire life

657
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:41,640
was defending alongside you.

658
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:46,880
You're my idol.

659
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:51,200
If there's a next life,

660
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:53,510
I'd still want to...

661
00:29:55,440 --> 00:29:57,570
stand beside you at the defense table.

662
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:00,550
Now,

663
00:30:01,570 --> 00:30:03,200
I'm willing to accept

664
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:06,020
whatever fate has in store for me.

665
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,680
Thank you, Mr. Yuan.

666
00:30:20,790 --> 00:30:21,400
Goodbye.

667
00:30:59,030 --> 00:31:00,630
Respected Presiding Judge,

668
00:31:01,350 --> 00:31:02,410
Associate Judges,

669
00:31:03,780 --> 00:31:05,180
and People's Assessors,

670
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:07,420
the defendant in this case

671
00:31:08,350 --> 00:31:11,030
was among the first generation
of university students educated

672
00:31:11,030 --> 00:31:13,560
after the founding
of the People's Republic.

673
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:15,920
He could have made

674
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:18,400
greater contributions to our country.

675
00:31:19,830 --> 00:31:20,790
Sadly,

676
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:25,000
most of his life was spent

677
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,830
under abnormal circumstances,

678
00:31:29,550 --> 00:31:31,030
and as a result, the ambitions

679
00:31:31,030 --> 00:31:32,150
of his youth...

680
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:36,840
could never be realized.

681
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:39,440
In his personal life,

682
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:42,110
he could never face the true reality

683
00:31:42,110 --> 00:31:43,920
of his marriage.

684
00:31:44,750 --> 00:31:47,240
Years of avoidance and indifference

685
00:31:48,110 --> 00:31:50,310
tore apart the family he should have

686
00:31:51,110 --> 00:31:53,000
devoted himself to maintaining.

687
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:56,440
And in his old age,

688
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,350
he murdered his own wife.

689
00:32:01,460 --> 00:32:02,790
It's truly lamentable.

690
00:32:04,030 --> 00:32:05,270
We condemn the defendant's

691
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:06,200
act of murder.

692
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,410
At the same time,

693
00:32:10,030 --> 00:32:11,640
we must also show him

694
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:15,240
the mercy and compassion of the law.

695
00:32:17,750 --> 00:32:19,110
We must let him know

696
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,240
that the law will not forgive

697
00:32:21,750 --> 00:32:23,080
the crime he committed,

698
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:26,770
but the law has also seen...

699
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:32,720
the suffering he endured.

700
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:38,240
Thank you.

701
00:33:00,510 --> 00:33:01,480
Has Xia Yingjie's martyr status

702
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:02,480
been decided yet?

703
00:33:03,590 --> 00:33:04,240
Oh, that.

704
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:06,590
The report was submitted long ago.

705
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:07,590
The leadership is still reviewing it.

706
00:33:07,590 --> 00:33:08,520
Reviewing what?

707
00:33:10,210 --> 00:33:11,310
The man's already in detention—

708
00:33:11,310 --> 00:33:13,840
just question him
and it's settled, isn't it?

709
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:16,280
Martyr recognition

710
00:33:16,310 --> 00:33:18,100
has standards and procedures.

711
00:33:18,620 --> 00:33:19,160
For instance,

712
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,000
was she carrying out

713
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:20,940
an official duty at the time...

714
00:33:20,940 --> 00:33:21,870
What do you mean?

715
00:33:23,310 --> 00:33:24,680
You mean once she left the courthouse,

716
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:25,960
it no longer counted as being on duty?

717
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:26,960
She was retaliated against years later,

718
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:29,440
and it isn't considered
a death in the line of duty?

719
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:30,270
If Xia Yingjie isn't a martyr,

720
00:33:30,270 --> 00:33:30,830
who is?

721
00:33:31,830 --> 00:33:32,680
You? Or me?

722
00:33:34,830 --> 00:33:35,550
Do you think Xia Yingjie

723
00:33:35,550 --> 00:33:37,010
wanted to become a martyr?

724
00:33:37,830 --> 00:33:38,350
Do you think her family

725
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:39,650
wanted that for her?

726
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:40,480
Yu Gaoyuan.

727
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:43,240
Don't make this personal.

728
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,570
I am making it personal.

729
00:33:46,420 --> 00:33:48,280
Court Pres. Qiu, I'm telling you—

730
00:33:48,490 --> 00:33:49,720
if Xia Yingjie died for nothing,

731
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:51,380
this won't be over between us.

732
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:17,159
[Beloved Daughter, Xia Yingjie]

733
00:34:19,610 --> 00:34:22,969
[Approved by the Dongjiang Provincial Government,
Xia Yingjie was posthumously awarded the title of Martyr.]

734
00:34:36,550 --> 00:34:37,210
Take a look.

735
00:34:37,389 --> 00:34:38,790
The exhumation results.

736
00:34:44,840 --> 00:34:45,600
Absurd, isn't it?

737
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:46,480
Look, isn't this absurd?

738
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:47,719
Look, it says right here.

739
00:34:47,719 --> 00:34:49,370
"After STR typing,

740
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:50,969
none of the three bloodstains

741
00:34:50,969 --> 00:34:52,480
on the bloody shirt
matched the genetic loci

742
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:54,110
taken from Yin Ping's remains."

743
00:34:54,110 --> 00:34:55,670
Not one of them matched!

744
00:34:56,150 --> 00:34:57,190
What's even more ridiculous is

745
00:34:57,190 --> 00:34:58,760
that the only DNA detected
was a mixed profile

746
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:00,410
belonging to Hu Xudong's brother and dad.

747
00:35:00,410 --> 00:35:01,150
There wasn't even

748
00:35:01,150 --> 00:35:02,710
a biological trace from Hu Xudong himself,

749
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:03,910
let alone Yin Ping's!

750
00:35:04,280 --> 00:35:06,610
Doesn't this prove Hu Xudong is innocent?

751
00:35:14,840 --> 00:35:15,400
Alright.

752
00:35:16,670 --> 00:35:18,400
At least we've found the truth.

753
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,320
Lu.

754
00:35:20,110 --> 00:35:21,240
You handle the rest.

755
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:23,770
I'm really exhausted.

756
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:21,960
Lihui.

757
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:29,280
Your mentor kept thinking about you

758
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:31,540
right up until he passed away.

759
00:36:41,710 --> 00:36:42,240
Mrs. Guo.

760
00:36:44,190 --> 00:36:44,800
Keep this

761
00:36:45,550 --> 00:36:46,030
safe.

762
00:36:49,510 --> 00:36:50,440
Your mentor said

763
00:36:51,150 --> 00:36:52,610
he wanted you to have this.

764
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:55,690
He left it to you.

765
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:57,720
Diandian.

766
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:01,440
Dad bought some braised beef.
Come out and eat.

767
00:38:04,230 --> 00:38:05,280
You're playing piano now?

768
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:07,610
How long has it been
since you last played?

769
00:38:09,140 --> 00:38:09,630
Mom,

770
00:38:09,630 --> 00:38:11,260
how do you think I'm playing?

771
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,570
Have I gotten worse?

772
00:38:13,590 --> 00:38:14,110
No.

773
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,330
I think you've actually improved.

774
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:38,880
Your dad has been

775
00:38:39,190 --> 00:38:41,390
losing sleep night after night lately.

776
00:38:42,190 --> 00:38:43,190
Even when he gets up to use the bathroom,

777
00:38:43,190 --> 00:38:44,920
he has to go to your room to check

778
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:46,990
to make sure you're still there.

779
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:48,510
I'm fine.

780
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:51,840
Seriously...

781
00:38:59,070 --> 00:38:59,890
When a person

782
00:39:01,470 --> 00:39:03,070
suffers an enormous loss,

783
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:06,200
sometimes the reaction doesn't

784
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:07,210
come right away.

785
00:39:08,710 --> 00:39:09,630
At first,

786
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:12,490
they may seem completely unaffected.

787
00:39:12,710 --> 00:39:14,190
They don't cry or seem sad.

788
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:15,760
And people around them might say,

789
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:17,400
"What's wrong with this person?

790
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:19,260
Why don't they seem upset at all?"

791
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,380
Actually,

792
00:39:21,710 --> 00:39:23,070
the pain comes later.

793
00:39:24,030 --> 00:39:25,560
I know what that feels like.

794
00:39:25,850 --> 00:39:26,550
When your grandpa

795
00:39:26,550 --> 00:39:27,400
passed away,

796
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:30,180
I didn't

797
00:39:31,190 --> 00:39:32,920
shed a single tear for 3 months.

798
00:39:33,190 --> 00:39:34,310
But 3 months later,

799
00:39:34,480 --> 00:39:35,210
I broke down.

800
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:36,960
I fell seriously ill.

801
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:35,000
Tian!

802
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:36,840
Tian!

803
00:40:37,670 --> 00:40:38,510
Auntie Wu.

804
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:39,850
Why are you here?

805
00:40:40,270 --> 00:40:41,110
My third aunt lives here.

806
00:40:41,110 --> 00:40:42,510
I just came over to visit.

807
00:40:43,190 --> 00:40:44,110
You guys take a break.

808
00:40:44,110 --> 00:40:45,070
Hurry up, hurry up.

809
00:40:45,070 --> 00:40:46,200
What a coincidence.

810
00:40:46,630 --> 00:40:47,320
Let me introduce you

811
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:48,070
to my son.

812
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:52,760
I'm sorry.

813
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,330
Yizhong!

814
00:40:55,400 --> 00:40:55,930
Yizhong!

815
00:40:57,960 --> 00:41:00,160
The Fifth Session of the Eighth

816
00:40:58,610 --> 00:41:01,290
[March, 1997]

817
00:41:00,210 --> 00:41:01,400
National People's Congress

818
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:02,960
has formally voted to adopt

819
00:41:03,190 --> 00:41:06,920
the "Criminal Law
of the People's Republic of China (Amendment)."

820
00:41:08,290 --> 00:41:10,110
This is the largest-scale revision

821
00:41:10,110 --> 00:41:11,800
since the first Criminal Law

822
00:41:11,820 --> 00:41:12,800
of the People's Republic of China

823
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:14,590
was promulgated in 1979.

824
00:41:15,810 --> 00:41:17,210
The new Criminal Law will

825
00:41:17,230 --> 00:41:19,370
officially take effect

826
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:20,460
on October 1, 1997.

827
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:23,100
It marks a significant step
toward a more scientific

828
00:41:23,100 --> 00:41:25,230
and standardized criminal justice system

829
00:41:25,230 --> 00:41:25,960
in our country.

830
00:41:25,390 --> 00:41:27,860
[Defendant Qin Zhigao, who had a duty to
rescue the victim, knowingly failed to act]

831
00:41:27,890 --> 00:41:30,990
[after the victim ingested highly toxic pesticide,
thereby showing indirect intent to let the victim die.]

832
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:29,670
This revision includes

833
00:41:29,670 --> 00:41:31,230
the following key breakthroughs:

834
00:41:31,030 --> 00:41:33,370
[His omission constituted intentional homicide,
and he was sentenced to 6 years in prison.]

835
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:32,410
First,

836
00:41:32,820 --> 00:41:35,760
it explicitly establishes
the principle of legality.

837
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:36,220
Second,

838
00:41:36,710 --> 00:41:38,190
it cracks down on new forms of crime

839
00:41:38,190 --> 00:41:39,990
and safeguards economic order.

840
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:41,400
Third,

841
00:41:41,790 --> 00:41:43,570
[Four months later, new evidence emerged
during the death-penalty review,]

842
00:41:41,890 --> 00:41:43,480
it restructures the Criminal Law

843
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:44,860
and restricts the use
of the death penalty.

844
00:41:43,570 --> 00:41:45,350
[prompting
the Dongjiang High People's Court to]

845
00:41:45,420 --> 00:41:48,990
[reject the death sentence,
acquit Hu Xudong, and release him.]

846
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:46,550
Fourth,

847
00:41:47,070 --> 00:41:49,870
it provides more detailed
sentencing standards.

848
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:54,590
Upon a lawful appeal
by the procuratorial authority,

849
00:41:54,590 --> 00:41:56,850
the court conducted a retrial and found,

850
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:58,590
upon examination, that the evidence

851
00:41:58,590 --> 00:42:00,590
supporting the original conviction

852
00:42:00,590 --> 00:42:02,510
of Yan Jicai for rape resulting in death

853
00:42:02,510 --> 00:42:04,000
was unsubstantiated.

854
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:05,960
The original judgment was
therefore vacated,

855
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:08,150
and Yan Jicai was acquitted.

856
00:42:09,280 --> 00:42:10,190
Meanwhile,

857
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:12,630
the procuratorial authority transferred

858
00:42:12,630 --> 00:42:13,440
the relevant leads and evidence

859
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:16,570
to the public security authority
for reinvestigation.

860
00:42:16,730 --> 00:42:18,480
The law enforcement personnel

861
00:42:18,510 --> 00:42:20,150
involved in Yan Jicai's case at the time

862
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:22,950
were held accountable
in accordance with the law.

863
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:53,920
[This series offers only a glimpse into a particular chapter
in the development of China's judicial system.]

864
00:42:53,950 --> 00:42:55,240
[Since its founding, our Party has attached great importance
to the rule of law. Under the strong leadership]

865
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:56,530
[of the CPC Central Committee, China's system
of people's justice has continued to move forward.]

866
00:42:56,560 --> 00:42:57,910
[A sound rule-of-law environment is
never built overnight.]

867
00:42:57,910 --> 00:42:59,260
[In the new era, China's commitment
to advancing the rule of law continues,]

868
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:01,390
[with ongoing efforts to improve the system and move steadily
toward greater fairness and standardization.]

869
00:43:02,500 --> 00:43:04,910
[The end]
